---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="The Power of Gaming — Krize Kster" description="The Power of Gaming by Krize Kster.">
  <section class="section-wrap grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[.8fr_1.2fr] lg:items-center">
    <div data-parallax="-0.06" class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm rounded-[.7rem_1.75rem_1.75rem_.7rem] bg-[#31433a] p-6 shadow-[1.2rem_1.2rem_0_#becbb9] sm:p-9">
      <div class="flex min-h-[29rem] flex-col justify-between border border-paper/35 p-6 text-paper sm:min-h-[35rem] sm:p-8">
        <p class="font-mono text-[.62rem] uppercase tracking-[.12em] text-mist">Krize Kster / 2025</p>
        <h1 class="text-[clamp(3.8rem,7vw,6.6rem)] font-extrabold leading-[.76] tracking-[-.12em]">The<br />Power<br />of<br /><span class="text-[#d5e0cb]">Gaming</span></h1>
        <p class="font-mono text-[.62rem] uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-mist">A book about systems, stories &amp; play</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Book / 04</p>
      <h2 data-parallax="0.04" class="mt-4 text-[clamp(3.8rem,8vw,8.4rem)] font-extrabold leading-[.79] tracking-[-.11em]">What games can teach us about building.</h2>
      <p class="mt-7 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed tracking-[-.035em] text-ink-soft">The Power of Gaming follows the systems that make interactive worlds memorable — and asks how their lessons can help us think differently about products, technology, and creative work.</p>
      <a href="#chapters" class="button button-dark mt-8">Explore the ideas <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="chapters" class="border-y border-line bg-[#e4e9df]">
    <div class="section-wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Inside the book</p>
      <h2 data-parallax="0.03" class="section-heading mt-3">Interactive worlds are carefully held systems.</h2>
      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-[1.35rem] border border-line bg-line md:grid-cols-2">
        <article class="bg-paper p-7 sm:p-9"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Worlds</p><h3 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-bold leading-[.95] tracking-[-.07em]">Why places players remember feel coherent.</h3><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">The rules, atmosphere, and small details that turn a collection of assets into a world with its own logic.</p></article>
        <article class="bg-paper p-7 sm:p-9"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Feedback</p><h3 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-bold leading-[.95] tracking-[-.07em]">Every action needs a meaningful response.</h3><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">How feedback loops invite attention, build trust, and create the feeling that an experience is truly alive.</p></article>
        <article class="bg-paper p-7 sm:p-9"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Story</p><h3 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-bold leading-[.95] tracking-[-.07em]">Narrative is structure, not decoration.</h3><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">A look at the frameworks that give choices, spaces, and characters a reason to matter together.</p></article>
        <article class="bg-paper p-7 sm:p-9"><p class="eyebrow">04 / Practice</p><h3 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-bold leading-[.95] tracking-[-.07em]">Bringing the lessons back to software.</h3><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Translating play, progression, and world-building into better digital products and creative processes.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
